Representation side-channel ledger
face         metric triple    payload                                          transfer
sum          (3, 1, 2)        terms, moments, cancellation order               Basel power sums; LRC pair sums; OCF coefficient sums
product      (2, 3, 1)        local factors, zeros, norm/sieve channels        sine/Wallis factors; Euler products; p-adic obstruction ledgers
fraction     (1, 2, 3)        convergents, continuants, boundary owner state   continued-fraction clocks; carry/owner derivatives; Euclidean descent
raw_decimal  (0, 0, 0)        scalar digits only                               diagnostic checksum; not a proof carrier

Tournament Analysis over representation faces
  vertices=sum, product, fraction, raw_decimal
  pairwise observable=which side channel is preserved better
  switch=gauge majority over additive_packet, local_factor, recursive_boundary
  tie Hamiltonian path=sum -> product -> fraction -> raw_decimal
  outscores={'sum': 2, 'product': 2, 'fraction': 2, 'raw_decimal': 0}
  score_hist={0: 1, 2: 3}
  directed_3cycles=1 [('sum', 'product', 'fraction')]
  sccs=[['fraction', 'product', 'sum'], ['raw_decimal']]
  hamiltonian_paths=3
  edges:
    sum -> product
    fraction -> sum
    sum -> raw_decimal
    product -> fraction
    product -> raw_decimal
    fraction -> raw_decimal

Assumption challenge
  Vertex candidates considered: values, formulas, terms, factors, convergents,
  proof lenses, side-channel types, LRC residues, OCF packets, and owner states.
  This script uses representation faces because the predicate is not numerical
  equality; it is which information survives scalar collapse.

Hypothesis update
  A scalar value should be stored as a trinity record when possible:
    sum packets + product factors + fraction boundary state.
  HYP-2229 already supplies the product-to-sum bridge through the sine product;
  S662 adds the missing fraction face as a recursive owner/convergent channel.
